# Compact replies

When answering in chat (questions, design discussion, reviews):

- **Length:** Prefer short, direct answers. One tight paragraph often enough; expand only when the user asks or the task needs it.
- **Spacing:** At most one blank line between sections. No large gaps between list items. Avoid “wall of whitespace.”
- **Structure:** Use small lists over multi-section essays. Skip wide tables unless the user needs comparison or many columns.
- **Bold/formatting:** Use sparingly — not every term.
- **Code citations:** Still use required `startLine:endLine:path` when referencing repo code; keep surrounding prose minimal.

Implementation tasks (steps, diffs, commit messages) stay complete and precise; compact does not mean omitting safety-critical detail.
